 piece for example the  most successful manga of all time each  of the main protagonists have a family  in some form although most of them are  dead but as a result they are allowed to  go out into the world to pursue their  dreams whilst in regards to living  family when applicable  well Luffy in 22 years of publication  has never even met his father so that  should give you a good indication of  that and no it's not that simple and  families used a great effect but it is  not the core idea of a series like one  piece but if we say move into the board  of Salem briefly then we do have an  example of a series where family is the  core idea which would be Full Metal  Alchemist the heart and soul of that  series has the brotherly bond between  Edward and Alphonse and the power of  that bond is powerful  throughout the run of the series leading  to incredible emotional highs and lows  it shows the incredible potential of  this broad idea and demon slayer takes  that and amplifies it to a global scale  and the most obvious parallel here is  the relationship between Tantra and  Nezzer Co which actually mimics the  Edward Alphonse relationship quite  closely with them being siblings on a  mission to restore the body of Nezzer Co  but this is the obvious one and I'm not  going to spend too much time on it as a  result but already just be aware that  family is the driving force of the  series from a protagonistic standpoint  however in a rather uncharacteristic  move especially for Shonen it is also  the core idea from the standpoint of the  antagonists in fact the introduction of  the series antagonist whose donkey-booty  suji didn't occur in the aftermath of  some giant battle or in a deep dark lair  plotting like many shown in series but  instead he was introduced to randomly on  the street with his family and that was  a great shock to the system of both  tandro and the audience you know the  whole how could this guy who slaughtered  my entire family be a decent-enough  existence to have a family of his own  and of course whether or not kyboot cg  actually cares for his family is almost  irrelevant it's more that this was how  he was introduced to tandra and the rest  of us as the antithesis of what we would  have thought he was prior to this moment  that is the simple power of adding the  idea of family into the mix even a  superficial one but with kyboot cg the  idea of family runs much much deeper  because the series goes to great lengths  to continuously state that all demons  are related to him and not only that but  some are closer relations than others  depending on if he sides him directly  and how much of his own blood was  provided to any particular demonic  individual so when a really twisted way  family is also what is driving the  antagonistic forces of the world as well  especially at the high levels filled  with demons constantly striving to own  kyboot suji's approval as if he were an  actual father figure but family also  comes out in the individual motives of  demons as well with probably the  greatest example of course being rui  whose character development took place  around the concept that he was searching  for his true parents because his human  parents attempted to murder him after  rui became a demon despite of course  loving him dearly and so he went about  crafting his own demonic family  essentially enslaving a whole host of  demons to act not only as his parents  but as his siblings and of course as  soon as rui sees the bond between tantra  and new Zucco he realizes that what he  has is absolutely nothing and goes on to  seek family in another  mana by assuming that taking a Zuko will  imprint that bond on to him by default  and now with all of that in mind what do  we think rui ends up being defeated by  yes you guessed it family despite being  more powerful than tandra Onizuka Rui is  overcome at least temporarily by their  familial bond however it wasn't just  Andrew anneza ko it was the whole  Commodore family unit you know in his  moment of need tonzura sought help from  their father and know Zuko was  encouraged by their mother resulting in  an absolutely impossible moment that  gave tandro the opening he needed and  this portion of the series is still  probably my favorite moment to date  which is also likely heavily influenced  by the spectacular anime adaptation of  it but it shows the power of family and  the incredible payoff that this idea can  have when implemented correctly but it  also isn't just an idea that's explored  within the main protagonists and  antagonists like I said earlier the idea  family is quite literally everywhere in  Demon Slayer and to demonstrate this we  can go all the way back to the early  phase of the series featuring Yoko ducky  and in this case his family bones were  with the orphaned children that he had  trained and rather sadly sent to the  early deaths as each and every one for  them failed the final selection and as a  result of this perceived failure as well  as Haruka Ducky's grief the souls of the  children remained in this world until  they were able to be put to rest by  tonzura and it's not as if the children  held any animosity towards arucard Aki  either with Malcolm or going so far as  to state that she loves him and that is  a familial bond at its finest and a  great example of how such a simple idea  can underpin an entire arc because  without this focus on family none of  this works the emotions would not be  strong enough to satisfactorily justify  spirit children and the euphoria of  defeating the demon that claimed them  would be just another in a long list of  generic shown and victories moving to  another more obvious example now and I  don't think we can really discuss the  brilliance of family without bringing  Zen e2 into the mix this seemingly  hopeless boy was relentlessly trained by  his grandfather and former ha Shura  jiguro khawaja MA  but despite the impossible task ahead of  him jiguro never gave up on Zen e2 and  he was thrilled when he was able to  master but one technique in regards to  Thunder breathing and this left a great  imprint on Xena too as a character who  desires more than anything to live up to  the effort that his grandfather put into  training him as well as the sheer amount  of belief that he had in him which is a  phenomena that he rarely experiences in  the world and it really does come to  define zenit too as well as his struggle  with cowardice and very much becoming  the only source of clarity going forward  family is a powerful thing after all and  in the case of the mighty you know sky  you could say that his character exists  as contrast to not only show the absence  of family but of the effect that  developing the most basic of connections  can have I mean yes I guess you know  escape was primarily raised by Bors so  he does have a UH a unique family will  say but in escape very much enters demon  slayer has a bit of a blank slate and as  a result of the bonds that he develops  with Tonto and everyone else he comes to  grow an awful lot as an individual and  it's all very obviously a result of  these close relationships that he's  developing and as a result he really  does serve as a perfect contrast  characters like Tonto and Xena too who  are well accustomed to the benefits and  detriments of family then there's also  Canal who has seen both the best and the  worst that family has to offer growing  up she lived in an incredibly abusive  environment to the point where she was  psychologically broken and even sold off  into slavery  however Canal was acquired by the cacio  sisters and that newfound sense of  family immediately and radically changed  her life and there are of course much  more subtle portrayals of family as well  such as the entirety of the hashira they  are all very purposely designed to evoke  a feeling of older siblings who have the  experience necessary to guide our  younger protagonists in this world and  you know what at first I was kind of put  off by the idea that all of the hashira  were essentially young adults because in  my mind you'd figure that the pinnacle  of power in this world might have a bit  more age and experience behind it  however instead they're all under 30 and  in fact most of them are barely into  their 20s but it is a very intentional  decision to portray them like this  because you know they have this really  cool vibe about them that younger  children have a tendency to feel towards  their older siblings because parents are  great and all but when you're a kid  there is nobody cooler in this world  than your older brother or sister so it  makes a lot of sense that the people  we're supposed to feel other course in  the world take on that familial role and  without going into spoilers most of them  to embody this idea to a fault when they  are eventually export in the series so  they do act as yet another wonderful  result of what happens when you put the  core concept of family into action and  of course all of this is just a tiny  portion of how family has influenced  every facet of demon slayer and going  forward that core concept is only going  to become more obvious and I believe  that that is why the series has struck  such a chord with people because firstly  family as stated before is an idea that  is almost never given heavy focus in  assurance series at least not as an  underlying concept  so as a result to Chernin fans demon  slayer feels really fresh and the  advantages of doing this idea properly  bring to the table impacts the readers  and watches in ways that they aren't  necessarily used to in one piece my hero  academia hunter hunter whatever it is  and just to be clear once again though  every other story I've mentioned does  effectively use family but it's done so  as more of a narrative accessory they  invoke family when it's necessary to  invoke family you know like during a  flashback or an urgent situation here  and there to give a character some  really solid motivation but none of them  use it as their prime factor and that's  not to say they should either every  successful series has its own reasons  and ideas that have led it to widespread  popularity and family just happens to be  demon Slayers bread and butter a series  could choose to focus on any number of  different concepts but the most  important thing is that they explore  them in depth and in a dramatically  impactful manner and demon slayer is  nothing short of a masterpiece in that  regard I think there are definitely  things to fault about Demon Slayer  especially after reading the manga but a  lot of it is nitpicky stuff and none of  it outweighs how marvelous a job the  series has done of what it set out to do  and you know what that core exploration  combined for the brilliant anime  adaptation well in that case I think  it's pretty inevitable that the only  option left for Demon Slayer was to go  on and take the world by storm and that  pretty much does it for the secret to  the success of Demon Slayer if you  enjoyed this video and the content this  channel produce in general then please  do consider donating to the new  worldview patreon because the support of  all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  support this channel an incredible  amount and if you'd like to join the fun  at any time then please do head over to  my discord server where a wide array of  shenanigan tree takes place on a daily  basis and finally please do comment with  your thoughts on family and Demon Slayer  this has been the new world of you and  I'll see you next time  you

